<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-section-InterpretDeriv" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Interpreting Derivatives</title>

  <p> Introduce the topic </p>

  <outcomes>
    <ul>
      <li>Find the (instantaneous) rate of change of the dependent variable with respect to the independent variable for a function y = f(x) that models a physical situation (e.g. volume as a function of time, volume as a function of radius), and state the units of instantaneous rate of change.</li>
      <li>Describe what information the sign of the derivative provides about the original function, in context of a real-world scenario.</li>
      <li>Translate between Leibniz notation, f' notation and written words to describe derivatives, in context of a real-world problem.</li>
      <li>Explain how Leibniz notation for the derivative relates to the slope interpretation. Use Leibniz notation to make sense of the units of the derivative.</li>
    </ul>
  </outcomes>
  

</section>